I'll update the `Iframe.vue` component to make it visible by default and update `WorkspaceAppLoader.vue` to use opacity control like `AppWindow.vue` does.

## Changes Summary

| File | Changes |
|------|---------|
| `src/components/Iframe.vue` | Remove `class="bg-base-300"` to keep iframe visible |
| `src/components/quick-chat/WorkspaceAppLoader.vue` | Add opacity control based on `isLoading` state, pass `app.path` to iframe `:url` prop |

```vue src/components/Iframe.vue
<template>
  <iframe ref="iframe" :src="url"
    @load="onIframeLoaded"
    title="coder" allow="camera *;microphone *;clipboard-read; clipboard-write;">
  </iframe>
</template>
<script>
export default {
  props: ['url', 'nocheck'],
  methods: {
    onIframeLoaded() {
      const { iframe } = this.$refs
      if (!iframe?.contentWindow) {
        return setTimeout(() => this.onIframeLoaded, 2000)
      }
      if (this.nocheck) {
        return this.$emit('loaded', iframe)
      }
      this.$emit('loaded', iframe)
    }
  }
}
</script>
```

```vue src/components/quick-chat/WorkspaceAppLoader.vue
<script setup>
import Iframe from '@/components/Iframe.vue'
</script>

<template>
  <div class="flex flex-col h-full w-full bg-base-100" :class="isLoading ? 'opacity-10' : ''">
    <!-- Header with app info and close button -->
    <div class="shrink-0 flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-3 border-b border-base-300/50 bg-base-100">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 min-w-0">
        <i
          v-if="appIcon"
          :class="appIcon"
          class="text-lg text-primary shrink-0"
        ></i>
        <span class="text-sm font-medium text-base-content truncate">
          {{ appName }}
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-1">
        <button
          class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm btn-circle text-base-content/60 hover:text-base-content"
          title="Close app"
          @click="$emit('close')"
        >
          <i class="fas fa-xmark"></i>
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Iframe container - always rendered, visibility controlled by opacity -->
    <div class="flex-1 overflow-hidden">
      <Iframe
        v-if="appUrl"
        :url="appUrl"
        :nocheck="true"
        @loaded="onIframeLoaded"
      />
    </div>

    <!-- Loading state overlay -->
    <div v-if="isLoading" class="absolute inset-0 flex items-center justify-center bg-base-100/50">
      <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-3">
        <span class="loading loading-spinner loading-md text-primary"></span>
        <span class="text-sm text-base-content/60">Loading {{ appName }}...</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Error state -->
    <div v-if="error" class="absolute inset-0 flex items-center justify-center bg-base-100/50">
      <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-3 text-center px-4">
        <i class="fas fa-circle-exclamation text-lg text-error"></i>
        <span class="text-sm text-base-content/60">{{ error }}</span>
        <button
          class="btn btn-sm btn-primary mt-2"
          @click="retry"
        >
          Retry
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  props: {
    app: {
      type: Object,
      required: true
    }
  },
  emits: ['close', 'loaded'],
  data() {
    return {
      isLoading: true,
      error: null,
      loadTimeout: null
    }
  },
  computed: {
    appName() {
      return this.app?.name || 'Workspace App'
    },
    appIcon() {
      return this.app?.icon || null
    },
    appUrl() {
      return this.app?.path
    }
  },
  mounted() {
    this.setupLoadTimeout()
  },
  beforeUnmount() {
    this.clearLoadTimeout()
  },
  methods: {
    setupLoadTimeout() {
      this.clearLoadTimeout()
      this.loadTimeout = setTimeout(() => {
        if (this.isLoading) {
          this.error = 'Failed to load app. Please try again.'
        }
      }, 15000)
    },
    clearLoadTimeout() {
      if (this.loadTimeout) {
        clearTimeout(this.loadTimeout)
        this.loadTimeout = null
      }
    },
    onIframeLoaded() {
      this.clearLoadTimeout()
      this.isLoading = false
      this.error = null
      this.$emit('loaded')
    },
    retry() {
      this.error = null
      this.isLoading = true
      this.setupLoadTimeout()
    }
  }
}
</script>
```

**Key changes:**
- **Iframe.vue**: Removed `class="bg-base-300"` to keep iframe always visible for workspaces to load
- **WorkspaceAppLoader.vue**: 
  - Moved iframe outside conditional rendering so it loads in background
  - Added `:class="isLoading ? 'opacity-10' : ''"` to parent div (similar to AppWindow approach)
  - Changed loading/error states to absolute overlays that appear on top

I'll review the current implementation and make necessary adjustments to ensure the loading animation shows while the app loads, and the AppWindow remains hidden until fully loaded.

## Analysis

The current implementation has a logical issue:
- The main container has `opacity-0` when loading, which hides the entire component including the loading spinner
- The loading overlay is positioned absolutely but may not be visible due to parent opacity

## Changes Required

